---
// /learn/frameql-an-introduction — hosts the v1.1 source (measure migration, 2026-08-03), byte-
// consistent with the Zenodo record. Title/subtitle from front-matter; the record's own DOI (21774643,
// version chain covers v1.1) and the vocabulary-move note are page chrome. Middle rung of the FrameQL
// ladder: /what-is-frameql (5 min) → this introduction (25 min) → the Manual (/docs/frameql). The
// ```frameql fences fall back to plaintext under the site's Shiki (no highlighter error).
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Content, frontmatter } from '../../content/corpus/frameql_an_introduction_v1_1.md';
const DOI = '10.5281/zenodo.21774643';
---
<BaseLayout title="Frame-QL: An Introduction — datumwise"
  description="The introduction to Frame-QL — the output frame is the query. Why rows, tables, joins, and GROUP BY are not primitives of the request interface, and where AI belongs at the intent boundary.">
  <div class="page-head">
    <p class="kicker"><a href="/learn">Learn</a></p>
    <h1 class="serif">{frontmatter.title}</h1>
    <p class="lede">{frontmatter.subtitle}</p>
    <p class="doi mono"><a href={`https://doi.org/${DOI}`} rel="noopener" target="_blank">doi.org/{DOI}</a></p>
  </div>

  <article class="prose">
    <Content />
  </article>

  <p class="evidence-note">
    <strong>Note, 2026-08-03.</strong> The theory's vocabulary moved again, and this time the move
    retired a word. <em>The Theory of Data</em>, Version 4.0
    (<a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21774032" rel="noopener" target="_blank">10.5281/zenodo.21774032</a>)
    replaces <em>atom</em> with <strong>measure</strong> — the governed family — because the old word
    named smallestness while the object is a family with laws. A column realizes a <strong>member</strong>:
    a governed <strong>series</strong>. The account is unchanged; a family is constituted by its law,
    and so, it turns out, is a vocabulary.
  </p>

  <p class="engage wayfinding">
    Lighter first: <a href="/what-is-frameql">What is FrameQL — and why?</a> ·
    The reference, complete: <a href="/docs/frameql">the FrameQL Manual</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-head { width: min(100% - 3rem, var(--measure)); margin: 0 auto; }
  .page-head h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 2.6rem); margin: 0.3rem 0 0.5rem; }
  .kicker a { color: var(--ink-faint); text-decoration: none; }
  .kicker a:hover { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .lede { font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .doi { font-size: 0.8rem; margin-top: 0.4rem; }
  .doi a { color: var(--ink-faint); }
  .evidence-note { width: min(100% - 3rem, var(--measure)); margin: 3rem auto 0; padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .engage { width: min(100% - 3rem, var(--measure)); margin: 1.5rem auto 0;
    font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
</style>
